1
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:31,240
He has a lot of fans.

2
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:32,479
You don't even know Jinxi?

3
00:00:32,479 --> 00:00:33,210
I don't know.

4
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:56,840
Stop.

5
00:00:58,920 --> 00:00:59,720
Bai Feixin.

6
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:01,880
You came in early. Why

7
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:03,080
did you keep singing?

8
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:04,480
And the music,

9
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:06,690
why did it keep playing?

10
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,180
Did no one notice the problem?

11
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,160
Director.

12
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:17,780
It's a problem that Feixin came in early.

13
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:18,680
But Heying,

14
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:19,940
why did you sing along?

15
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:22,050
Do you think it doesn't matter?

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:23,720
How many times have you two

17
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:24,920
rehearsed this song?

18
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,460
Are you tired of it?

19
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:28,680
No matter how many times

20
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:29,560
you've done it,

21
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:30,960
to the audience,

22
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:32,160
it's always the first time.

23
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,080
Understood?

24
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:35,120
Did you hear me?

25
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,479
Understood.

26
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,080
Bye, director.

27
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:48,680
Here we go again.

28
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,060
Starting what?

29
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,759
Today is

30
00:01:51,759 --> 00:01:52,680
the last

31
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,880
performance of "Jianjia".

32
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:56,160
Then we'll start rehearsing Nie Xiaoqian.

33
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:57,440
"A Chinese Ghost Story".

34
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:58,440
Every time

35
00:01:58,440 --> 00:01:59,960
we transition from old to new,

36
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,420
you get really irritable.

37
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:02,600
Do I?

38
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:03,200
Don't you?

39
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,680
Even your legs aren't as stiff

40
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,010
as your stubborn mouth.

41
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:09,120
They said you're not going to the dinner tonight.

42
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,000
Why not?

43
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
What will you do staying home alone?

44
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:16,140
"One Hundred Years of Solitude".

45
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,440
It's not like we're splitting up after this show.

46
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:22,100
We'll still be working together on the next one.

47
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,520
Today's performance was a great success.

48
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:25,520
That's exactly why we need to relax.

49
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,520
That's why we should celebrate, right?

50
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:29,040
Don't be so tense.

51
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,640
I don't like going to group dinners.

52
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,480
It's not with us.

53
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,220
Do you remember Kevin?

54
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:38,400
Kevin has a very good friend joining us today.

55
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,040
He's a top-tier executive.

56
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,040
Ning Jin.

57
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:43,690
What are you going home for?

58
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:44,720
Are you going to spend the rest of your life

59
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:45,760
with your cat?

60
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:49,320
That actually sounds pretty good.

61
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,120
It's better than finding an unreliable man.

62
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,079
That really won't do.

63
00:02:52,079 --> 00:02:52,600
Why not?

64
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:54,440
How long has it been since you dated someone?

65
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:55,079
How long has it been

66
00:02:55,079 --> 00:02:57,079
since you felt that flutter,

67
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:59,160
that heart-pounding sensation,

68
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:00,960
or butterflies in your stomach?

69
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,680
I just don't get butterflies in my stomach.

70
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:05,940
And I think I'm doing just fine like this.

71
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,280
I'm heading back.

72
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:10,400
Anyway, I saw someone online say

73
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,520
that the romance in "Jianjia"

74
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:12,400
is a bit bland.

75
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,200
Who said that?

76
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:15,680
Find it and let me see.

77
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:16,560
I don't know.

78
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:19,490
There are also follow-up comments agreeing with it.

79
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:20,980
Which comment?

80
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:22,079
Show it to me.

81
00:03:22,079 --> 00:03:22,940
Does it matter?

82
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:25,570
Who always tells us during rehearsals

83
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:27,320
that art comes from life?

84
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,520
Rehearsals for 'A Chinese Ghost Story' are about to start.

85
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,850
Have you figured it out?

86
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:32,160
How to write the romance between

87
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:33,890
Nie Xiaoqian and Ning Caichen?

88
00:03:34,079 --> 00:03:36,160
Why don't you awaken the butterflies

89
00:03:36,320 --> 00:03:37,250
in your stomach?

90
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,680
If you wait any longer,

91
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,680
they'll get too old to flutter.

92
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,360
The feeling of a heartbeat.

93
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,440
Thump-thump.

94
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:44,800
The feeling of love.

95
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,880
Thump-thump.

96
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:51,960
I'm sorry.

97
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:53,160
I lied about keeping you company.

98
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:54,520
I won't be a third wheel.

99
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,280
I'm going to a dinner party.

100
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,160
Have fun!

101
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,560
I knew it.

102
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:58,640
What's wrong?

103
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:00,600
Nothing.

104
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,920
What do you think of this place?

105
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:09,480
It's pretty good.

106
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:10,760
Did you notice?

107
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:12,890
The one singing on stage is Mochou.

108
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,600
A friend of mine opened this place.

109
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,680
It's members-only.

110
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,200
Many celebrities like to come here.

111
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,800
You people in the art circles

112
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,680
should like it here.

113
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,080
I'm not in any art circle.

114
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,160
Directing is my profession.

115
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:28,880
It's not for playing around.

116
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:31,090
You're very assertive.

117
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,800
I like it.

118
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:35,159
I have quite a few director friends.

119
00:04:35,159 --> 00:04:36,159
They told me

120
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:38,170
that people in your profession

121
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,770
have a strong desire to create.

122
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:41,400
Right?

123
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:43,720
I guess so.

124
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:46,880
Then I hope all your desires

125
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:48,840
can be satisfied.

126
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,000
This cocktail

127
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:04,040
isn't very strong.

128
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:12,920
Drink this.

129
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:19,360
This will make it much stronger.

130
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,020
Bottoms up.

131
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:22,360
No.

132
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:00,960
Thank you.

133
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:02,850
You're welcome.

134
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:07,960
Miss Ning.

135
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,600
Director.

136
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:12,280
You are so beautiful.

137
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:17,880
I know I am beautiful.

138
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:20,640
But do you know

139
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:22,400
what a beautiful female director

140
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:23,160
after entering the industry

141
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:24,240
must learn first?

142
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,200
What is it?

143
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:28,440
Don't get yourself too drunk.

144
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,400
So you won't be

145
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,920
taken advantage of by

146
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:33,840
some greasy middle-aged investors.

147
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:34,640
No,

148
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,200
what do you mean?

149
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,280
With your alcohol tolerance,

150
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,940
even if you take me away today,

151
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,260
you can't do anything.

152
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,560
Why don't you go back

153
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,560
before you black out?

154
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:55,360
Okay.

155
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:58,260
What are you doing?

156
00:06:58,800 --> 00:06:59,680
Sorry.

157
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,160
Stop pretending.

158
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,480
How is my heart

159
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:07,810
supposed to skip a beat?

160
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,600
What on earth am I doing?

161
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:48,000
Come to my office right away.

162
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,080
Jin Xi?

163
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:51,800
Yes.

164
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:52,960
Jin Xi.

165
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:55,280
Why are you

166
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:57,160
looking at me so confused?

167
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:58,730
You don't even know him?

168
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:00,400
Why do I need to know who he is?

169
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:02,160
You have to know who he is.

170
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:03,280
Jin Xi.

171
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,440
He's the music industry's

172
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:05,770
hottest star right now.

173
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,960
As a shot in the dark,

174
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:09,480
I called his management team.

175
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:10,120
I didn't expect

176
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,680
his management team to be so interested in this.

177
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,160
If Jin Xi comes,

178
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:16,360
for the 20 shows of 'A Chinese Ghost Story',

179
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,320
I could sell out 21 shows,

180
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:20,720
and won't even have to give the theater manager a kickback.

181
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,680
Wait a minute.

182
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:26,290
Does he have any experience performing in musicals?

183
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:29,120
Ning Jin.

184
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:32,690
Don't smile at me like that.

185
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,480
Every time you smile at me like that,

186
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,010
nothing good ever happens.

187
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:42,880
Ning Jin.

188
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:47,320
Well,

189
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:49,200
she is

190
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:51,720
the most popular singer nowadays.

191
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:54,340
With that singing skill and popularity,

192
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,880
could I arrange things blindly?

193
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:01,560
Go sit over there.

194
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:08,600
Lao Wu.

195
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:13,080
A singer and a musical actor are two different things.

196
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,600
If he doesn't have stage experience,

197
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,530
it's impossible for me to train him

198
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,040
to be the male lead of a musical

199
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,100
in just two months.

200
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,440
I understand.

201
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:24,200
When we signed the contract,

202
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,200
I promised you

203
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:28,240
that I would never interfere with the creative process.

204
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,720
But this great opportunity

205
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,720
fell from the sky,

206
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:31,920
we have to catch it.

207
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:34,600
Tonight,

208
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:37,520
his manager wants to treat me to a late-night snack.

209
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:38,920
The singer is coming too.

210
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,140
Don't refuse just yet.

211
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,340
Let's give it a try.

212
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,080
Jin.

213
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:47,520
Give me a chance.

214
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:50,840
Okay?

215
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:52,720
Jinxi! Jinxi!

216
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:54,400
Never leave you!

217
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:56,040
Jinxi! Jinxi!

218
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:58,560
Love you forever!

219
00:10:59,120 --> 00:10:59,800
Jinxi,

220
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:01,520
where are you?

221
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:03,040
Let us see you!

222
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:08,480
Let me tell you,

223
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,520
our Jinxi

224
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:10,480
is fully booked

225
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:11,720
for a long time.

226
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,120
But he just loves musicals,

227
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:15,720
has loved them since childhood,

228
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:17,480
and insisted I get him one.

229
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:18,200
So here we are,

230
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,640
he's going to be in a musical.

231
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:22,120
Nothing compares to passion.

232
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:23,960
When I told

233
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,240
our director about this,

234
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:27,440
he couldn't stop smiling.

235
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:28,800
The director also told me

236
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:31,330
that rehearsing a play is like fighting a war,

237
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:33,640
and actors are the weapons.

238
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,080
If you have a handy weapon,

239
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:38,160
there's no battle you can't win.

240
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:40,280
If the director is Guan Yu,

241
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:43,120
your Jinxi is Diaochan—

242
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:43,800
no,

243
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,360
the Green Dragon Crescent Blade.

244
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:47,800
Isn't this a match made in heaven?

245
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,840
I brought the stamp to sign with you.

246
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:51,640
It's a deal.

247
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:52,800
What deal?

248
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:57,000
I am the only one

249
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:59,160
who has the final say on the lead actor I wrote.

250
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,360
I haven't even met

251
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:01,200
this actor yet.

252
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,730
What are you deciding here?

253
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,560
But this is Jinxi.

254
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:06,080
Sorry,

255
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:08,210
I don't really listen to pop music.

256
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,920
And I don't want to decide the lead actor

257
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,320
just because of a dinner.

258
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,080
Excuse me.

259
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:14,360
This is a live performance,

260
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:15,000
a stage.

261
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,530
I must see him in person.

262
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:22,280
Ning Jin

263
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:24,600
is the backbone of our troupe.

264
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:28,800
I highly respect her creative work.

265
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:30,240
Boss Wu,

266
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:32,720
that's not what we agreed on before.

267
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,920
I don't care what Lao Wu told you.

268
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,240
But

269
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,840
to play Ning Caichen,

270
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:39,920
he must attend the audition.

271
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,170
I'm done eating.

272
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,500
I'll take my leave.

273
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:47,200
Director.

274
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:48,660
I'll take my leave as well.

275
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:49,300
This...

276
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:55,840
Director, can we start?

277
00:12:58,560 --> 00:12:59,360
Director.

278
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:01,080
Director.

279
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:06,040
Please start your performance.

280
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,160
Start.

281
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:15,480
Four is four, ten is ten,

282
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,840
fourteen is fourteen,

283
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,360
forty is forty.

284
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:19,480
Stop.

285
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:24,480
We don't have a tongue twister segment.

286
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,640
I learned this for a web drama

287
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:27,920
from a teacher I hired before.

288
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:29,680
He said I'm really good at tongue twisters.

289
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:31,400
I also prepared a kissing scene.

290
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:32,530
No, an action scene.

291
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,640
No need for the action scene.

292
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:38,440
Just start your song selection.

293
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:40,080
